            {
                "entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                "word": "publicain",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "407dab1b-1d3c-49af-b8b1-7d75ddf189ee",
                        "entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "publicains"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "74114040-129f-4317-a627-b1e6088b3247",
                        "entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                        "tags": [
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "publicaine"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a6987fdf-e307-3354-8f1e-ac71e20ee780",
                        "entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fermier des deniers publics, chez les Romains."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ancient"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "60d71b00-1862-4682-8ddb-82952cb2cdd5",
                                "sense_id": "a6987fdf-e307-3354-8f1e-ac71e20ee780",
                                "text": "Les gens de cette profession étaient odieux parmi les juifs ; l’Évangile dit : il faut le traiter comme un païen et comme un publicain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b32391e7-49d8-4c23-a645-b1ea50f28e15",
                                "sense_id": "a6987fdf-e307-3354-8f1e-ac71e20ee780",
                                "text": "Sans fléchir ses genoux en écartant les jambes, elle se courba si bien que son menton frôlait le plancher ; et les nomades habitués à l’abstinence, les soldats de Rome experts en débauches, les avares publicains, les vieux prêtres aigris par les disputes, tous, dilatant leurs narines, palpitaient de convoitise."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99093b3d-aa9b-4f5b-b378-e9c4dc4f240e",
                                "sense_id": "a6987fdf-e307-3354-8f1e-ac71e20ee780",
                                "text": "La rapacité des publicains se donnait libre carrière dans les provinces. Partout où les armes romaines avaient pénétré, ils s’abattaient sur le pays et le mettaient en coupe réglée."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a543c67d-6199-361c-8134-81995e59cd01",
                        "entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Collecteur subalterne juif, au service de l’occupant romain, détesté par la population locale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Ancient",
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "58c28527-909a-3f48-8662-4db0a236ca9e",
                        "entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Percepteur, collecteur, financier, ou quiconque est chargé de percevoir les deniers publics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea7f623e-337b-453f-b939-949e70b5c41a",
                                "sense_id": "58c28527-909a-3f48-8662-4db0a236ca9e",
                                "text": "Les compagnies de négociants, de financiers, de traitants, de publicains et d’accapareurs donnent toujours naissance à une foule de courtiers, d’agents de change et d’agioteurs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2d771ef-ad2f-4cc6-9fa7-df9372096fc1",
                                "sense_id": "58c28527-909a-3f48-8662-4db0a236ca9e",
                                "text": "Pour les péages dûment érigés un certain nombre de règles s’imposaient. Les publicains devaient avoir sur le port des tableaux publics portant la liste des marchandises sujettes aux droits et le taux de la perception, entretenir un homme en permanence sur le ponton afin que les voituriers sussent à qui parler. — (Pierre Lenail, Le parlement de Dombes, Lyon 1523 à 1696 - Trévoux 1697 à 1771, Bernoux & Cumin (éds), Lyon, 1900, page 32)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0ca1a11-ff00-4fb0-bf55-b4d4db0cf458",
                                "sense_id": "58c28527-909a-3f48-8662-4db0a236ca9e",
                                "text": "Fallait-il que j’attende plusieurs heures encore, voire jusqu’au lendemain, que des policiers passent par là — les rosses publicains, comme disait Zwakh en parlant d’eux ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8fa4997-baee-459a-bfda-461afa9b7d26",
                                "sense_id": "58c28527-909a-3f48-8662-4db0a236ca9e",
                                "text": "Lâchons, lâchons, lâchons ! Lâchons la grappe à nos frères. Sont-ils homosexuels ? Ils auront leur place, avant nous, dans le Royaume des Cieux. Ils se marient ? T’inquiète, dans le Royaume, y a de la place pour deux. L’un des deux se prostitue ? Pas de souci, frangin, le président Jésus, comme le nomme affectueusement le père de l’Église Basile de Koch (XXIᵉ siècle après JC), habite généralement chez les putes. Ou chez les publicains. Les publicains, sait-on vraiment aujourd’hui dans une France qui n’est largement pas allée au catéchisme, ce que cela veut dire ? Ce sont les percepteurs d’impôts… Cela fait deux mille ans qu’ils n’ont pas bonne presse —les Évangiles nous en sont témoins…"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5b4fd1a0-60fc-33f0-8f54-578accc46553",
                        "entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Personne cupide, avare, vénale, qui cherche à faire du profit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2e0f81c-53e6-403b-b44a-386ef070face",
                                "sense_id": "5b4fd1a0-60fc-33f0-8f54-578accc46553",
                                "text": "BAREBONE\nAyez soin en frappant d’épargner ces rideaux !\nFaites, si vous pouvez, qu’il tombe sur le dos ;\nDe sorte que le sang de ce Moloch visible\nSur mes tapis d’Alep coule le moins possible.\nNouvelle explosion d’indignation parmi les conjurés.\nSYNDERCOMB, regardant Barebone de travers.\nQuel est ce publicain ?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e5a997d5-75ea-4585-97ff-e29528383b11",
                        "source_entry_id": "4e21cede-5477-3e67-89dd-d765f6c8ce2d",
                        "target_lang_word": "publican",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "publican",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c00dc6b-bf22-3b21-aed1-b4e550f42cbe",
                                        "entry_id": "226c1765-cc31-32ac-8ed5-d574439592af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The landlord (manager or owner) of a public house (“a bar or tavern, often also selling food and sometimes lodging; a pub”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85646a55-3425-4813-bada-57c159234e9c",
                                                "sense_id": "0c00dc6b-bf22-3b21-aed1-b4e550f42cbe",
                                                "text": "I went into a public-'ouse to get a pint o' beer, / The publican 'e up an 'sez, 'We serve no red-coats here.'"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5539eec1-1a58-391d-924e-40f5c8c6257e",
                                        "entry_id": "226c1765-cc31-32ac-8ed5-d574439592af",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The manager or owner of a hotel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Commonwealth",
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "publican",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                        "entry_id": "ddba7d11-8fd3-3f22-8e55-75745a74388d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tax collector, especially one working in Judea and Galilee during New Testament times (1st century C.E.) who was generally regarded as sinful for extorting more tax than was due, and as a traitor for serving the Roman Empire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ancient-Rome",
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "031baa2d-aad3-40a4-9335-15f0c21061aa",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "Matthevv vvhiche vvas other vvyſe alſo called Leui, beyng of a Puplican made an Apoſtle, firſt of all others compoſed and vvrote in Jevvrye, the ghoſpell of Chriſte in the Hebrue tounge, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcdd8e3a-2578-4505-b3b1-7c33023dcb8a",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "[T]he Publicans, that is to ſaye, the cuſtomers and takers vp of tolles, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bccfb008-b03d-4448-9771-361329ceda03",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "Hovv like a favvning Publican he lookes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52cc8b51-dbc8-42ec-9e9a-e6c334581fde",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "[I]f he [a brother who trespasses against one] neglect to heare the Church, let him be vnto thee as an heathen man, and a Publicane."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24264c03-52c2-48fc-86d5-25742a14b9c1",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "[T]here was a man named Zacheus, which was the cheefe among the Publicanes, and he was rich."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d2593aa-6d16-4a3f-b800-84e22c1ccb5c",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "The provinces groaned at once under all the severity of publick imposition, and the rapaciousness of private usury. They were overrun by publicans, farmers of the taxes, agents, confiscators, usurers, bankers, those numerous and insatiable bodies, which always flourish in a burthened and complicated revenue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68c6de78-307c-4492-89d0-2bbbc600a695",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "Now, Mrs. Varden, […] believing, moreover, that the publicans coupled with sinners in Holy Writ were veritable licensed victuallers; was far from being favourably disposed towards her visitor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb5afa01-c4e7-4b78-9a95-ea2208849279",
                                                "sense_id": "5d636f5a-2553-3c5d-ab9f-a4e225fadf1f",
                                                "text": "He brings twelve men with him, fishermen, tillers of the soil, one a publican, all of the humbler class; and he and they make their journeys on foot, careless of wind, cold, rain, or sun."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11c400a5-02ee-3364-8e7f-e63dc6ba86c1",
                                        "entry_id": "ddba7d11-8fd3-3f22-8e55-75745a74388d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any person who collects customs duties, taxes, tolls, or other forms of public revenue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "245c4a32-a9fd-41ac-967e-b4dec2761abd",
                                                "sense_id": "11c400a5-02ee-3364-8e7f-e63dc6ba86c1",
                                                "text": "Another ſort there be vvho vvhen they hear that all things ſhall be order'd, all things regulated and ſetl'd; nothing vvritt'n but vvhat paſſes through the cuſtom-houſe of certain Publicans that have the tunaging and the poundaging of all free ſpok'n truth, vvill ſtrait give themſelvs up into your hands, mak 'em, & cut 'em out vvhat religion ye pleaſe; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8a1c9d2-7e8e-4122-8f6d-67fbdfd140c7",
                                                "sense_id": "11c400a5-02ee-3364-8e7f-e63dc6ba86c1",
                                                "text": "[…] I am fallen into the hands of Publicans and Sequeſtrators, and they have taken all from me, vvhat novv? let me look about me. They have left me the Sun and the Moon, Fire and vvater, a loving vvife, and many friends to pity me, and ſome to relieve me, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70d5748d-727f-4c49-b7d0-68cdf3af4957",
                                                "sense_id": "11c400a5-02ee-3364-8e7f-e63dc6ba86c1",
                                                "text": "Nor could the Treasury effectually restrain the chimneyman from using his powers with harshness: for the tax was farmed; and the government was consequently forced to connive at outrages and exactions such as have, in every age, made the name of publican a proverb for all that is most hateful."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f09d17cf-39e6-308e-8a50-4ce3d7f2bba9",
                                        "entry_id": "ddba7d11-8fd3-3f22-8e55-75745a74388d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One regarded as extorting money from others by charging high prices."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89271d77-f609-3c8b-af0d-b1b8b0d02dd5",
                                        "entry_id": "ddba7d11-8fd3-3f22-8e55-75745a74388d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person excommunicated from the church; an excommunicant or excommunicate; also, a person who does not follow a Christian religion; a heathen, a pagan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
